The following is a list of different armor types and the benifits in armor
class that they gain you.  Certain items may have other advantages that
are not discussed here.  Anything that can rust is preceeded by an "R".
Any item can have plusses over and above this list.  If the item is known
by another name until identified that other name is listed.  The items
are grouped by types, and there may be a list of names preceeding the list
in which case the names are mapped onto the items randomly upon starting
the game.

	Boots					Lowers AC

(Riding, Snow, Hiking, Mud, Jungle)
	  Fumbling				1
	  Levitation				1
	  Jumping				1
	  Elven					1
	  Water Walking				1

	  Low (walking)				1
	  High (jack)				2
	R Iron (hard)				2

	Gauntlets

	(padded, old, riding, fencing)
	  Fumbling				1
	  Leather				1
	R Power					1
	  Dexterity				1


	Cloaks

	  Elven (ornamental cope)			1
	  Orcish (black mantlet)			0
	  Dwarvin (colorful hooded)			0
	  Protection (tatered cape)			3
	  Invisibility (opera hood)			1
	  Magic Resistance (faded pall)			1
	  Displacement (piece of cloth)			1

	Helms

	(Crested, Plumed, Visored, Rusty pot)
	R Helmet					1
